[h1]Turn every meal into a kitchen story[/h1]
Cooks gather tools, diners fetch settings, meals cool, and somebody washes up.

[b]RimWorld 1.6[/b]

[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/10557042170922753510/EE9080A68BAB28F9053DB9C2DBD7BED228910F66/[/img]

[h1]What changes[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Stuff-aware kitchenware[/b] - Material, quality and dirt matter.
[*][b]Physical meal service[/b] - Most meals use kitchenware.
[*][b]Dishwashing and sanitation[/b] - Used gear returns dirty and needs washing.
[*][b]Ingredient preparation[/b] - Prep cooks fast but spoils quickly.
[*][b]Cooperative cooking[/b] - Linked cooks help the chef.
[*][b]Culinary quality[/b] - Ingredients, skill, tools and service all count.
[*][b]Meal temperature and reheating[/b] - Food cools and can be reheated.
[*][b]Dining standards[/b] - Wealth and rank raise expectations.
[*][b]Travel, guests, children and patient feeding[/b] - Each gets sensible tableware.
[*][b]Nutrient paste[/b] - Bring a plate; paste can also be an ingredient.
[*][b]Trade and world-generated meals[/b] - Outsiders may bring packed tableware.
[/list]

[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/10595014367887970089/07F935B974C098924B64F63F2B2D009BEDA574D9/[/img]

[h1]New things[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Primitive stone cookware set[/b] - Cheap early-game pots and pans.
[*][b]Cookware set[/b] - Reusable pots and pans in many materials.
[*][b]Glitterworld cookware set[/b] - Rare self-cleaning gear.
[*][b]Plate and adobe plate[/b] - Reusable plates from wood to precious metal.
[*][b]Cutlery setting[/b] - Stackable knives, forks and spoons.
[*][b]Chef's knife set[/b] - Personal tools for equipped cooks.
[*][b]Prepared ingredients[/b] - Fast-cooking food with a short shelf life.
[/list]

[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/9402614076826008064/6F61AD9217541F194847E28F8AE5DF0EA13A2426/[/img]

[h1]New buildings[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Dishwasher[/b] - Cleans batches and resumes after interruptions.
[*][b]Industrial dishwasher[/b] - Handles busy kitchens.
[*][b]Ingredient prep station[/b] - Prepares food before the rush.
[*][b]Sauce station[/b] - Adds a linked cook's speed and skill.
[*][b]Meat station[/b] - Supports recipes with a specialist cook.
[*][b]Vegetable station[/b] - Adds skill to linked cooking.
[*][b]Pastry station[/b] - Supports demanding recipes.
[*][b]Microwave[/b] - Reheats cold meals on a table or workbench.
[/list]

[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/17722103090486615794/BBAF198C868232E50C00F051F680A766441B25FF/[/img]

[h1]Little rules that make it feel alive[/h1]
Pemmican and survival meals stay hand food. Animals skip forks. Meals return their own tableware. Dirty tools work in an emergency.

[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/15319281986753242149/1394EBA094EB853E3E71249E8F3B581900348911/[/img]

[h1]Required Mods[/h1]
[list]
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url][/b] - Runtime code patching; load it before Core.
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2574315206]XML Extensions[/url][/b] - Package-ID-aware compatibility patches; load it after Core and before Immersive Chefs.
[/list]

[img]https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/14006664955242215432/B9A0FEB55759677B102509FFD8D30A4C149D81EA/[/img]

[h1]Recommended Mods[/h1]
[list]
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=836308268]Dubs Bad Hygiene[/url][/b] - Adds plumbed dishwashers and sinks.
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3210544395]Processor Framework[/url][/b] - Runs dishwasher cycles and progress.
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1561769193]Common Sense[/url][/b] - Diners and nurses tidy used settings.
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1279012058]Pick Up And Haul[/url][/b] - Collects nearby dishes in batches.
[*][b][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3486264784]SBZ Fridge[/url][/b] - Loads after Adaptive Storage Framework ([url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3033901359]Workshop page[/url]); meals chill or freeze quickly, thaw slowly, and lose more quality after freezing.
[/list]

[h1]Optional Mods[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Royalty[/b] - Nobles expect finer dining.
[*][b]Biotech[/b] - Self-feeding children dine normally.
[*][b]Expanded Materials - Metals[/b] - Adds suitable metal choices.
[*][b]Expanded Materials - Masonry[/b] - Adds suitable stone choices.
[*][b]Ceramics (Continued)[/b] - Adds porcelain plates.
[*][b]Simply Sublime ABS Polymer[/b] - Adds plastic tools.
[*][b]Gastronomy[/b] - With Cash Register, waiters serve, warm and clear settings.
[*][b]Hospitality[/b] - Guests borrow colony tableware.
[*][b]Cook for Yourself[/b] - Personal cooks gather tools.
[*][b]Variety Matters[/b] - Variety and culinary quality work together.
[*][b]Vanilla Food Variety Expanded[/b] - Added ingredients remain visible.
[*][b]Dynamic Meal Texture Replacer[/b] - Meal looks survive saves.
[*][b]Food Texture Variety[/b] - Core loads before main; matching VCE add-ons keep meal art.
[*][b]Vanilla Expanded Framework[/b] - Supports Vanilla Expanded food mods.
[*][b]Vanilla Textures Expanded - Variations[/b] - With Vanilla Expanded Framework, adds variations.
[*][b]Vanilla Nutrient Paste Expanded[/b] - With Vanilla Expanded Framework, paste uses plates.
[*][b]Adaptive Meal Bill[/b] - Adaptive bills use the same kitchen rules.
[*][b]Meals on Wheels Continued[/b] - Delivery preserves tableware.
[*][b]Replimat / Replimat Meals[/b] - Replimat loads before its Meals add-on; diners bring plates.
[*][b]Vanilla Cooking Expanded[/b] - With Vanilla Expanded Framework (and Fishing for Sushi), meals join in.
[*][b]Fried Meals[/b] - With Harmony and Vanilla Expanded Framework, meals join in.
[*][b]Fast Meals[/b] - Fast recipes stay fast.
[*][b]Prioritize Meals over Preserved Foods[/b] - Food priorities stay intact.
[*][b]RimCuisine 2[/b] - Processor Framework loads before Core, then modules; meals join in.
[*][b]Meal Printer[/b] - Printed meals receive safe plate handling.
[*][b]RimFridge[/b] - Meals chill or freeze quickly, thaw slowly, and lose more quality after freezing; plates stay attached.
[*][b]Adaptive Storage Framework[/b] - Stored meals keep tableware.
[*][b]Overcooked Meals[/b] - Burnt meals keep plate rules.
[*][b]No Vanilla Meals[/b] - Removed vanilla meals leave no broken rules.
[*][b]Thermodynamics - Hot Meals[/b] - Its heat system and microwave take over.
[/list]

[h1]Languages[/h1]
English, German, Spanish, French, Simplified Chinese and Russian are included.

[h1]Author's Note[/h1]
This mod was completely developed by AI, supervised by me. I am a professional software developer and wanted to try using my experience and processes with agentic engineering for developing mods. A big focus was on creating frameworks for maintainability, testability and performance testing, which should help with maintaining compatibility with many mods and future RimWorld versions. I'll probably open-source the framework later if it proves itself, so other modders can use it as well. The mod does not generate AI content while RimWorld is running.

The mod itself was chosen for its complexity. It is a sweet spot of adding assets and new behaviours, but also having to be compatible with many other mods and DLC. It is a proving ground for more complex mods in the future. Be aware that while this is tested more thoroughly on a technical level than most, if not all, other mods, it is playtested much less heavily than usual. Feel free to comment on the balancing and any other oddities you encounter. I'll read them and implement the feedback.
